id: pm-slack-standup-7t31
title: Require exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage and strict quality gates
description: "The current V8 coverage gate measures only index.ts at 90.44% lines, 88.38% branches, and 91.79% functions, with no separately reported statements result. release:check now enforces canonical pm-ops ESLint lint and zero-duplication checks plus the docstring gate, but executable scripts remain outside coverage and the mutation and broader static/security gate criteria remain incomplete. This blocks an all-source 100/100/100/100 or production-ready claim."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: coverage,quality-gate,release-blocker,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-21T10:11:53.131Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T21:23:29.863Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every executable TypeScript and JavaScript source; replace or explicitly justify JavaScript; measure statements, branches, functions, and lines across every executable source at exact 100 percent; make the gate fail when a source is added or removed from measurement; add strict lint, duplication and security/static gates with no blanket suppression; mutation-check the gate; keep tests behavior-driven and non-duplicative"
definition_of_ready: Current release gate and source inventory are measured on main.
reviewer: greptile
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-quality
release: future
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: "main 2d0077a, Node V8 coverage"
repro_steps: Run npm run coverage and inspect coverage-gate DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS plus package thresholds.
expected_result: All executable repository source is measured at exact 100/100/100/100 and every strict quality gate is mandatory.
actual_result: "The 2026.9.28 CLI/SDK certification candidate passes 206 tests, 81 documented declarations, and zero duplicated lines. Coverage still reports only index.ts at 90.44/88.38/91.79 (lines/branches/functions), with no separate statements result. Mutation and broader security/static gate acceptance remain open."
affected_version: pm-slack-standup 2026.8.17
component: quality and release gates
customer_impact: "A green release gate can coexist with untested source and below-mandate coverage, so it cannot support a production-ready claim."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-22T05:10:25.678Z",pi-agent,"Not closed by the 2026.9.21 certify task pm-slack-standup-add0. That task delivers the canonical pm-ops lint and duplication gates only. This item still requires exact 100/100/100/100 all-source coverage, mutation checking, and the broader security/static analyzers named in its acceptance criteria."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T11:48:16.531Z",codex,CodeRabbit exact-head review verified that the description still carried the older 89.66/87.74/90.76 baseline. This append-only update aligns the blocker description with the final measured 89.97/88.32/91.27 result without changing its open status.
  "2026-09-28T21:07:57.383Z",codex,"2026-09-28 certification candidate (pm-slack-standup-74w8): release gate now runs canonical pm-ops lint, duplication and docstring checks, but V8 coverage still reports only index.ts at 90.44% lines, 88.38% branches, 91.79% functions; no independently reported statements dimension or whole-source coverage. This open item remains the readiness blocker. The package upgrade PR does not claim 100/100/100/100."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
